OL,3,GNEWSAFish swim upstream for first time
OL,4,Ain 20 years
OL,5,
OL,6,FA wetlands project which included the
OL,7,Fremoval of a weir from a Bradford beck
OL,8,Fhas resulted in fish swimming upstream
OL,9,Ffor the first time in 20 years.
OL,11,FThe fish returned to Pitty Beck in
OL,12,FAllerton just an hour after the weir,
OL,13,Fwhich was built in 2005, was taken away
OL,14,Fas part of a scheme to naturalise the
OL,15,Fflow of water.
OL,17,FThe project, which created new wetland
OL,18,Fareas to enhance biodiversity and
OL,19,Freduce flood risk, was a partnership
OL,20,Fbetween the Environment Agency, Aire
OL,21,FRivers Trust and West Yorkshire
OL,22,FCombined Authority.
OL,23,APub: 18-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
